# Decode, Calibration and Diagnose Packages for CEPC ECAL Beam Test Data

Yuzhi, CHE
Jiaxuan, WANG

## KEKCC

Code: /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/analysis/ECAL_Analysis_LCIO
Raw data: /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/ECAL_data/data
Analysis results: /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/ECAL_data/analysed
The active calibration factors remain in
data_beamtest/simulation/CEPCScECAL_SML_Portable_update_new/Analysis_edit/share.

Build with a matching ROOT/GCC environment (root-config and g++ must be available):

  make -C /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/analysis/ECAL_Analysis_LCIO

Edit year, beam, date_tag and energy in run/global_config before processing.
The existing defaults (2023, sps, e-, all) and factor filenames are unchanged.
Paths are resolved from the configuration file, so Bash scripts can be started
from another directory:

  bash /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/analysis/ECAL_Analysis_LCIO/run/decode.sh

The decode output is analysed/<year>/<beam>/decode/<date_tag>/<energy>/.
Calibration output is analysed/<year>/<beam>/calib/<date_tag>/<energy>/.
No symlink to an old server is required. Use bash, not sh, for these scripts.

The existing batch branches in calib/simpleCalib/SSA/track submit one LSF job
per input file with bsub. They create output/ before submission, request one
CPU, and use the default s queue. The existing simpleCalib energy=all branch
still executes directly. For example, after editing global_config:

  bash /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/analysis/ECAL_Analysis_LCIO/run/calib.sh
  LSF_QUEUE=l bash /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/analysis/ECAL_Analysis_LCIO/run/calib.sh
  bjobs

LSF_QUEUE overrides the queue for these drivers. At KEKCC, s has a 150-minute
CPU limit / 300-minute run limit; l has 1200 / 2400 minutes. Both have a 4 GB
memory limit. Logs are run/output/<stage>.<job-ID>.out and .err. The MC drivers
use run_simulation/output/; threshold scan retains its condition subdirectories.
The submitting ROOT/GCC environment is inherited by LSF jobs.

decode.sh and the pedestal scripts still execute directly. To put the complete
decode loop into one job, use the existing wrapper:

  cd /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/analysis/ECAL_Analysis_LCIO/run
  mkdir -p output
  bsub -q s < execute_analyzer_decode.sl

The .sl filenames are retained, with LSF #BSUB directives. These directives are
read by bsub only for stdin submission; drivers pass all options explicitly
when invoking an argument-taking wrapper with bash. The array wrappers are
templates with a sample sleep command, not analysis drivers. They now use
LSB_JOBINDEX (1-based) and logs containing job ID and array index.

For a single calibration without submitting a job, set a concrete energy in
global_config, source that file in Bash, and run the executable directly:

  source /gpfs/group/ilc/users/murata/data_beamtest/analysis/ECAL_Analysis_LCIO/run/global_config
  mkdir -p "$calib_path"
  "$bin_dir/calib" "$decode_path/<run>.root" "$pede_factor" "$inter_factor" "$mip_factor" "$calib_path/<run>.root"

Replace <run> with the chosen input basename. This retains the existing factor
files and calibration algorithm. No batch jobs are submitted by configuration.

Legacy inputs:
- pedestal_pedestal.sh uses the existing backup/seino_config (2025 KEK settings).
  Those settings are preserved; the 2025 data are not present in this copy.
- pedestal_nonpedestal.sh retains an existing "evho" command in energy=all;
  this branch does not run pedestal processing. The direct decode/pedestal
  loops also do not reliably propagate processor failures to their wrappers.
  These existing processing issues are outside the scheduler conversion.
- hl_ratio.sh is an old cosmic-ray helper using /mnt2/ScECAL_CR and ./main.
  Its original input data and executable are absent; do not use it as the
  current HG-LG intercalibration entry point without supplying those inputs.
- shift/ is a separate 2022 workflow; see shift/README.txt for its limitations.
